Fri Oct 16 16:44:37 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 4.4:
  * New comment-dwim on M-;, sort-lines, reverse-region,
    delete-duplicate-lines, transpose-lines, whitespace-cleanup,
    fill-region, tabify/untabify and delete-trailing-whitespace
  * New previous-buffer/next-buffer on C-x and the arrow keys,
    kill-current-buffer, rename-buffer and minibuffer history per
    prompt kind; the minibuffer now reads keys through the editor
    keymap, so word motions work there too
  * New display-line-numbers-mode, m4-mode and cmake-mode;
    makefile-mode highlights automake conditionals
  * New delete-selection-mode and ido-mode substring completion at
    prompts, both on by default
  * New auto-revert-mode (on by default) and auto-revert-tail-mode
    to follow a log like tail -f; revert-buffer keeps the line in
    every window showing the buffer
  * New sentence commands M-a/M-e/M-k and C-x DEL,
    recenter-top-bottom on C-l, move-to-window-line-top-bottom on
    M-r, where-is and describe-key on C-h w/k, and the IBM CUA
    S-Delete/C-Insert/S-Insert cut, copy and paste keys
  * New secure mode (-S) and single-file mode (-s) for restricted
    shells; --with-modes, --disable-syntax, --disable-help and
    --disable-autorevert to cut features for small builds
  * Fix shell command injection when opening a .gz file whose name
    contains shell metacharacters
  * Fix query-replace, replace-string and the regexp replace
    commands corrupting UTF-8 text, and isearch missing matches
    when the pattern has non-ASCII letters
  * Fix M-d/M-DEL and upcase-word undo on words with non-ASCII
    letters; words are now split by Unicode class
  * Fix shift, control and Meta with the arrow keys, Home, End,
    PgUp/PgDn, Insert and Delete in rxvt and urxvt
  * Fix a line over 127 bytes in ~/.mg silently ending the load
  * Fix C-x C-k to C-x C-x bindings shifted by one in builds
    without dired, and --disable-ctags ignored while cscope was on
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes
    for the full list

- Apply mg-keyseqname-ncurses-clash.patch: the keyname() helper
  4.4 added for where-is clashes with the keyname(int) that ncurses
  declares in curses.h, so the build fails wherever configure finds
  ncurses/curses.h; upstream fixed this the same way right after
  tagging 4.4

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Sep 16 17:34:49 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 4.1:
  * UTF-8 editing in UTF-8 locales, with double-width CJK and
    emoji measured per Unicode 17
  * Syntax highlighting (font-lock-mode) for C, shell, Python,
    Markdown, YAML, git-commit, diff, conf, makefile, and text
  * Visual mark mode; shift-arrow and shift-PgUp/PgDn selection
  * Side-by-side windows (C-x 3), windmove, and balance-windows
  * New line-wrap-mode (off by default)
  * git-commit-mode with Magit-like C-c C-c / C-c C-k
  * meta-key-mode off by default so 8-bit input works
    out of the box
  * use-short-answers on by default; new require-final-newline
  * Sync with OpenBSD (Mar 2026): replace-regexp infinite loop,
    scratch-buffer save prompt, memory leaks, and -flto externs
  * Fix ~/.mg errors being hidden on the echo line (issue #41)
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes
    for the full list
- Spec cleanup:
  * Use %autosetup; drop Group and autoreconf (release tarball
    ships configure)
  * Ship %{_datadir}/mg/tutorial.gz for C-h t

